course: dictionary
lesson: 7957
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A receiver is something or someone that takes in what is sent to it. The word comes from «receive», which means to get something that has been given or sent.
explain: Context shows you which meaning you need. «A remote-control car's controller sends radio signals that a receiver in the car turns into commands» tells you the receiver is a device. «A gift usually becomes the receiver's for keeps» tells you the receiver is the person who gets the gift.
explain: Sport uses the word too. A receiver is the player who catches the ball. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence: «the person who gets the gift» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A receiver is the part of a phone you hold to your ear and speak into.
fact: A receiver is a device that picks up radio or TV signals.
fact: In sport, a receiver is a player who catches or receives the ball, such as in American football or tennis.
fact: In money and law, a receiver is a person put in charge of a company that cannot pay its debts.
fact: Phrases to know: «pick up the receiver» and «a radio receiver».
exercise: «A remote-control car's controller sends radio signals that a receiver in the car turns into commands.» What is the receiver in this sentence? | A small motor that spins the wheels | *A device that picks up signals and turns them into commands | A person who owns the car | A device that picks up signals
exercise: «A gift usually becomes the receiver's for keeps.» What is a receiver in this sentence? | *The person who gets the gift | The box the gift came in | A shop that sells gifts | A card with a message
exercise: In sport, what does a receiver do? | Kicks the ball over the net | *Catches or receives the ball | Blows the whistle | Keeps the score
test: Which part of a phone do you hold to your ear and speak into? | *The receiver | The screen | The battery | The lid
test: What is a receiver in money and law? | A gift for a friend | A device that picks up radio signals | A player who catches the ball | *A person put in charge of a company that cannot pay its debts
exam: «A satellite TV dish collects weak signals and focuses them onto a receiver.» What does the receiver do? | *Takes in the signals the dish focuses onto it | Makes the dish face south-east | Stores the signals for later | Sends signals up to the satellite
